<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Travancore–Dutch War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1739">1739</a>–1753</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Travancore–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Dutch War</a> was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> and the kingdom of Travancore under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marthanda-varma">Marthanda Varma</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malabar-coast">Malabar Coast</a> of south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Travancore defeated a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> force at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-colachel">Battle of Colachel</a> in 1741, one of the first defeats of a European army by an Indian state. The Treaty of Mavelikkara of 1753 ended Dutch political ambitions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/travancore-dutch-war.jpg" alt="Travancore–Dutch War" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Infocaster at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:De_Lannoy_Surrender.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
